.\" Hand-written sections of improv-server(1); crates/cli/src/man.rs adds the rest.
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B improv-server
serves one model over HTTP/1.1 as JSON: read the model and measures, compute
what-if edits through the live engine, and write input cells. It listens on
.I addr
(default 127.0.0.1:3000, or
.BR IMPROV_ADDR ).
.I model
defaults to
.IR improv.db .
.PP
A model is a store file made by
.BR improv (1),
or a Postgres model URL,
.BI postgres:// user @ host / db ?model= name\fR.
.SH ROUTES
.nf
GET  /health                 liveness, no token needed
GET  /model                  the whole model
GET  /measures               id, name, kind, categories
GET  /measures/:id/values    stored inputs or computed values
POST /measures/:id/eval      what-if edits; "persist": true writes through
POST /measures/:id/cells     set one input cell
POST /nl/parse, /nl/describe controlled English to formula and back
GET  /scheduler/status       refresh scheduler state
.fi
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.BR IMPROV_API_TOKEN ", " IMPROV_API_TOKENS
Read-write bearer tokens (one, or comma-separated).
.TP
.B IMPROV_API_TOKENS_RO
Read-only bearer tokens.
.TP
.B IMPROV_ALLOW_OPEN=1
Allow running without a token on a non-loopback address (otherwise the
server refuses to start).
.TP
.B IMPROV_SCHEDULER=1
Refresh external-function measures in the background. It runs only functions
whose digest is listed in the file named by
.BR IMPROV_EXTFN_ALLOW .
.TP
.B IMPROV_ADDR
The address to listen on when no
.I addr
argument is given.
.TP
.B IMPROV_EXTFN_ALLOW
The allowlist file for the scheduler: one lowercase hex SHA-256 of
.IR name \e0 body
per line.
.TP
.B IMPROV_SCHEDULER_TICK_SECS
The scheduler's tick period (default 5).
.TP
.B IMPROV_HEADER_TIMEOUT_MS
Header read timeout (default 10000).
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
IMPROV_API_TOKEN=secret improv-server sample.db
curl -H 'Authorization: Bearer secret' localhost:3000/measures
.fi
.SH AUTHOR
Greg Burd <greg@burd.me>
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR improv (1),
.BR improv-files (5),
.BR improv-formulas (7),
.BR improv-tui (1),
.BR improv-gui (1).
